From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:12:15 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS] Fix re-entrancy UAF in WebMediaPlayerMS audio and video
 reload

SetNetworkState() synchronously notifies the client, which can run script
that modifies the MediaStream's tracks (re-entering Reload()) or tears
down the player via Shutdown(). Calling SetNetworkState() before
updating audio_renderer_ or video_frame_provider_ allowed an outer call
to overwrite a renderer started by a nested Reload() without stopping
it, leaving a dangling pointer registered with the track.

This CL:
- Updates ReloadAudio(), ReloadVideo(), and ActiveStateChanged() to
stop/replace renderers before calling SetNetworkState(), and guards
against Shutdown() clearing client_ during notifications.
- Defers web_stream_.AddObserver() in Load() until after
frame_deliverer_ and the initial renderers are set up.
- Calls Stop() in ~TrackAudioRenderer() and
~MediaStreamVideoRendererSink() so started renderers always disconnect
from their tracks on destruction.

Bug: 580846651, 578656065
Change-Id: Iefc7cd5b32257b593dd27537176f9ba71a31f8a0
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8714660
Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron <kron@chromium.org>
